        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Section 11.6 Temporary Military Leave. An employee who is a member of a reserve component of the Armed Forces, who is absent due to required active annual training duty or temporary special services duty, shall be paid his or her normal straight time earnings, including shift differential where applicable, up to a maximum of 80 hours each military service fiscal year. The amount due the employee under this 11.6 shall be reduced by the amount received from the government body identified with such active or temporary special duty, for the period of such duty (up to the maximum period mentioned above). Such items as subsistence, uniform and travel allowance shall not be included in determining pay received from the state or federal government. An employee who elects to work or use available vacation credits while on temporary active duty shall not be eligible for military pay differential for that period.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
